# {{.Name}}

An agentbus agent, generated by `agentbus agent init`. It builds to a
single static binary with its manifest and scripts inside.

```text
agent.yaml          what it serves, and which handler runs for each
handlers/*.go       Go handlers, compiled in (register with agent.Register)
scripts/            shell, Python or other scripts, embedded
main.go             entry point; leave as is
deploy/{{.Name}}.service   systemd unit
```

## Try it without building

On a machine with a broker and the `agentbus` CLI:

```bash
agentbus config agent add {{.Name}} --capability {{.Name}}.wordcount --capability {{.Name}}.disk
agentbus agent run -f agent.yaml      # Go handlers need a build; the others run as-is
```

## Build and deploy

```bash
agentbus agent build --target linux/amd64,linux/arm64     # writes dist/
scp dist/{{.Name}}-linux-amd64 host:/tmp/
```

On the broker host, `agentbus config agent add` (above) wrote the agent's
token to `~/.config/agentbus/tokens/{{.Name}}.token`. Copy it to the
remote host as `/etc/agentbus/{{.Name}}.token`, mode 0600, and install the
unit in `deploy/`. Check a host before starting the service:

```bash
AGENTBUS_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/agentbus/{{.Name}}.token {{.Name}} -check
```

## Handlers

Each handler in `agent.yaml` has one trigger and one action:

| Trigger | Means |
|---|---|
| `task: CAP` | take work from the capability's queue; one agent serving it gets each task |
| `inbox: true` (+ `op: NAME`) | answer requests sent to this agent; with `op`, only those whose `body.op` is NAME |
| `event: FILTER` | run on matching events from other agents; no reply |

| Action | Means |
|---|---|
| `run: COMMAND` | a shell command |
| `script: scripts/FILE` | a script, run by `interpreter:` or by its extension (.sh, .bash, .py) |
| `go: NAME` | a Go function registered with `agent.Register` |

Commands and scripts get the envelope JSON on stdin and print the reply
on stdout. `AGENTBUS_FROM` is the sender (checked by the broker),
`AGENTBUS_OP` the body's op, and `AGENTBUS_BODY` the body for small
messages. Exit 3 with `{"code": ..., "reason": ...}` on stdout to refuse
with that error; any other failure sends a generic error, and stderr stays
in the agent's log.

Everything in a message comes from another agent. Check its shape before
using it, and never pass it to a shell unquoted.
